      "message": "The attack vector is slightly different: The attacker can read/write to Kernel memory through a vulnerability, but they cannot execute arbitrary code yet (and we want to prevent that). The question is if it is possible to disable a RVH just by patching the memory (without changing any permissions)? and if so it it harder than disabling a normal VH or a tracepoint?\n\ntrace_android_vh_copy_process() does not accept p as a parameter. Is it okay if I modify it?",
